    "section": "Styling",
    "slides": [
        {
            "id": "s_l4_1",
            "type": "text",
            "title": "Dynamic Classes with :class",
            "content": "You can bind `class` using an object or an array.\n\n**Object syntax**: toggle classes based on data.\n\n```html\n<div :class=\"{ active: isActive, 'text-danger': hasError }\"></div>\n```\n\n**Array syntax**: apply multiple classes from an array.\n\n```html\n<div :class=\"[activeClass, errorClass]\"></div>\n```"
        },
        {
            "id": "s_l4_2",
            "type": "code",
            "title": "Example: Toggle Classes",
            "content": "A simple button that toggles an 'active' class:",
            "codeSnippet": "<div id=\"app\">\n  <div :class=\"{ active: isActive }\" @click=\"isActive = !isActive\">\n    Click me to toggle active class\n  </div>\n  <style>\n    .active { background-color: #42b983; color: white; padding: 20px; cursor: pointer; }\n    div { padding: 20px; border: 1px solid #ccc; cursor: pointer; }\n  </style>\n</div>\n\n<script>\n  createApp({\n    data() {\n      return { isActive: false };\n    }\n  }).mount('#app');\n</script>",
            "codeLanguage": "html",
            "canRunCode": true
        },
        {
            "id": "s_l4_3",
            "type": "text",
            "title": "Inline Styles with :style",
            "content": "Bind inline styles using an object (camelCase keys) or an array of objects.\n\n```html\n<div :style=\"{ color: activeColor, fontSize: fontSize + 'px' }\"></div>\n```\n\nYou can also bind to a computed property that returns a style object."
        },
